## First Bad Version (monotone binary search)

Everything after the first bad version is also bad → monotone → binary search.
- Inclusive range `[lo, hi]` with `lo <= hi` and `end = n-1`-style bounds.
- mid bad  → answer is mid or earlier → `right = mid`
- mid good → answer is after mid      → `left = mid + 1`
```cpp
while (start < end) {
    int mid = start + (end - start) / 2;
    if (isBadVersion(mid)) end = mid;
    else start = mid + 1;
}
return start;
```
Iterative is preferred here: O(1) space vs O(log n) for the recursive version.

